  "extract": "Daniel H. Pink is an American non-fiction writer who has authored seven New York Times bestsellers. He was host and a co-executive producer of the National Geographic Channel social science TV series Crowd Control. From 1995 to 1997, he was the chief speechwriter for Vice President Al Gore.",
  "extract_html": "<p><b>Daniel H. Pink</b> is an American non-fiction writer who has authored seven <span><i>New York Times</i> bestsellers</span>. He was host and a co-executive producer of the National Geographic Channel social science TV series <i>Crowd Control</i>. From 1995 to 1997, he was the chief speechwriter for Vice President Al Gore.</p>"
